# Delegate-model review EVIDENCE PACKETS (ai-grok-review, ai-glm, ai-muse, ai-qwen).
# The wrappers build this directory in the working tree to hand the reviewer the
# change under review. It is session scratch and must never be committable.
#
# This was previously ignored ONLY by `.git/info/exclude`, which is machine-local
# and is not part of the repository, so a fresh clone or any other machine would
# have offered the packet as an untracked commit candidate. The line below is
# NOT redundant with `.ai-review*.txt` above: that pattern matches a FILE named
# `.ai-review<something>.txt`, and the packet is a DIRECTORY containing
# MANIFEST.md and patch.diff.
.ai-review/

# Delegate-model review reports (ai-glm, ai-grok-review, ai-deepseek-agent).
# The wrappers refuse to write a report unless this path is ignored, because a
# NEW review is session scratch and must never be committable.
#
# THE EXCEPTIONS BELOW ARE DELIBERATE AND MUST NOT BE DELETED (#1304).
# 25 reviews were committed on purpose, across 14 separate commits, BEFORE this
# rule existed, and they are CITED BY PATH from permanent records that can never
# be edited: `supabase/migrations/20260729180000_revoke_anon_execute_style_
# tracker_and_cover_procedures.sql` names one in its header, and so do
# `docs/security/public-schema-execute-audit.md`,
# `docs/status-snapshot-and-change-log.md`,
# `docs/verification/production-apply-set-and-rehearsal-20260809.md` and a PopSG
# owner-approval record. Removing them breaks about a dozen citations in the
# permanent record and leaves the reasoning behind settled decisions readable
# only in Git history.
#
# Nothing automated reads them: the production evidence gate uses a checksummed
# workflow artifact, not these files. The loss would be the written record of WHY,
# which is exactly the thing that cannot be reconstructed later.
#
# A session reading only the line above once ran `rm -rf .ai` on the strength of
# it and deleted all 25. They were restored from Git, but only because `git
# status` was read. The list is here so the next session cannot make that
# mistake: what is tracked is named, and everything else stays scratch.
#
# DO NOT add new entries here. A new review is scratch. If a review must become
# permanent evidence, copy it to `docs/` under a name that says what it decides.
.ai/reviews/*
!.ai/reviews/20260729-public-execute-lockdown-glm.md
!.ai/reviews/20260802-taxonomy-alert-ack-rpc-glm52.md
!.ai/reviews/20260809-a2b-rehearsal-rerun-codex.md
